 35S     34S(N,G) E=THERMAL            1985RA15                  ENSDF    202509
 35S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$          
 35S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35S 2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35S  dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 17-Jul-2025)          
 35S  c  1985Ra15: 6|*10{+11} n/cm{+2}/s thermal neutrons at the target position
 35S 2c  were produced from the Los Alamos Omega West Reactor at a nominal 8-MW 
 35S 3c  reactor power. |g rays following thermal neutron capture by a 1.09-g,  
 35S 4c  77.7% enriched {+34}S target were detected using a 26 cm{+3} coaxial   
 35S 5c  Ge(Li) detector inside a 20-cm-diam by 30-cm-long NaI(Tl) annulus with 
 35S 6c  FWHM=2.3 keV at 1 MeV, 5.5 keV at 6 MeV and 8.8 keV at 11 MeV. Measured
 35S 7c  |s{-|g}, E|g, and I|g for 61 |g-ray transitions. Deduced 22 levels and 
 35S 8c  |g-ray branching ratios.                                               
 35S  c  1972Dz13: Thermal neutrons were produced from the thermal column of the
 35S 2c  IRT reactor of the Baghdad Nuclear Research Institute. |g rays         
 35S 3c  following thermal neutron capture by a 1.5-g, 97%-enriched {+34}S      
 35S 4c  target were detected using a 10-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector with FWHM=3.5   
 35S 5c  keV at 1 MeV and 8 keV at 7 MeV. Measured E|g and I|g for 22 |g-ray    
 35S 6c  transitions. Deduced 11 levels.                                        
 35S  c  1985Ke08: 5|*10{+12} n/cm{+2}/s thermal neutrons were produced from the
 35S 2c  McMaster University Reactor. |g rays following thermal neutron capture 
 35S 3c  by a natural sulfur target were detected using a 10% efficient Ge      
 35S 4c  centered within a NaI(Tl) annulus with FWHM=3.2-4.4 keV at 4-7 MeV.    
 35S 5c  Measured E|g and I|g for 13 |g-ray transitions. Deduced 9 levels.      
 35S  c  1997Be42: Thermal neutrons were provided from the reactor BR1 of the   
 35S 2c  Studiecentrum voor kernenergie in Mol, Belgium. |g rays following      
 35S 3c  thermal neutron capture by a 313.6-mg, 93.26%-enriched {+34}S and      
 35S 4c  5.933%-enriched {+36}S target were detected using a Ge detector.       
 35S 5c  Measured |s{-|g}, E|g, and I|g for 11 |g-ray transitions. Deduced 8    
 35S 6c  levels. Compared with direct-capture (DC) model calculations.          
 35S  c  All 55 E|g values from 2007ChZX: database of prompt gamma activation   
 35S 2c  analysis (PGAA) from neutron capture are in agreement with the data    
 35S 3c  below. Others: 2000Re01, 2001ZhZZ.                                     
 35S  cG $Photons per 100 thermal neutron captures are reported in 1972Dz13 and 
 35S 2cG 1985Ke08. |g-ray cross sections in mb are reported in 1985Ra15,        
 35S 3cG multiplying these by 0.340 yields the number of photons per 100 thermal
 35S 4cG neutron captures. |s(4638)=163 mb {I15}. I|g(4638)=|s(4638)|*0.340=55  
 35S 5cG {I5}.                                                                  
 35S  cG $|g-ray intensities per incident neutron for all transitions and |g-ray
 35S 2cG cross sections in mb for primary transitions are reported in 1997Be42. 
 35S 3cG The strongest 4638|g is used for normalization. |s(4638)=148.6 mb {I55}
 35S 4cG and I|g(4638)=|s(1997Be42)/|s(1985Ra15)|*I|g(1985Ra15)=50 {I7}.        
 35S  cG E,RI$From 1985Ra15, unless otherwise noted.                            
 35S  cG E(P)$Not observed in 2007ChZX (PGAA).                                  
 35S  cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies.                         
